cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PlotTrellis, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
title: "PlotTrellis: Composable Genomic Track Visualisations for Non-Coders"
version: 1.1.0
abstract: >-
  A plotgardener-based genomic track composer that lets biologists build
  common EDA visualisations (coverage, Hi-C, splice junctions, transcript
  structure, protein domains) via a Shiny interface, without writing code,
  and download a standalone R script that reproduces the exact figure
  offline.
authors:
  - family-names: Pacnik
    given-names: Aleksander
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-4062-2582"
    affiliation: "Walter and Eliza Hall Institute of Medical Research (WEHI)"
license: Artistic-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/aleks-wehi/PlotTrellis"
url: "https://aleks-wehi.r-universe.dev/PlotTrellis"
keywords:
  - R
  - bioinformatics
  - Shiny
  - genomics
  - visualisation
  - plotgardener
  - genome browser
  - RNA-seq
  - ATAC-seq
  - Hi-C
